## PREP boundary

There are 40 scenarios: 20 byte fixtures (four output views each) and 20 filesystem,
ByteIO and actual-Shell scenarios. Native capture has 109 observations, of which 80
are the content views. These are NOT 109 product tests/passes. Product runs: zero.
Twenty fixture files total 1394 bytes. Native only sees generated temporary files,
their directory/links/mode-000 fixture, and explicit supplied stdin. No native file
invocation sees repo files or private files. Native input is bounded to 65536 bytes;
each subprocess has a 3-second watchdog and 65536-byte output cap. No decompression
flags, native mock product, downloaded binaries, installed packages or custom magic.

Primary references were captured at the FILE5_41 upstream tag before any candidate
inspection/invocation. Full bytes and hashes are retained. Native is Apple/Darwin
file-5.41 with an explicitly selected magic database; it is not a GNU/Linux oracle
or proof that Apple's binary is byte-identical to upstream FILE5_41. The capture
timestamp proves when this verifier captured evidence, NOT an unobserved author's
start time. Root must establish any cross-agent before-implementation chronology.

No author files, author tests, root exports, package metadata, defaults or existing
dispatch code were inspected. Only user instructions, prior discovery checkpoint,
contracts, and the readFile/readStream bodies in current Memory/Real FS were used.
No candidate module is imported by any PREP file. All imports are builtins or the
