## Reporting and failure routing

Each content row preserves all four raw candidate results. Native-exact lane tests
MIME/encoding bytes/status/stderr; human prose is semantic-only, with original native
human text retained as reference. Frozen alias sets do not erase exact-native
conflicts. Partial Unicode, PDF charset, empty/gzip aliases, truncated PNG and
JPEG's malformed length are explicit profiles, not demands for full libmagic parity.

Workflow native lanes stay not-run unless actually compared: never fabricate a
profile conflict or a pass for an unperformed comparison. F30/F31 can demonstrate
safe backend refusal but remain backend-limitation, NOT successful classification.
Status aggregation must preserve `fail`, `unsupported`, `native-profile-conflict`,
`backend-limitation`, `oracle-unavailable`, `harness-defect` and `not-run` as distinct
from `pass`. Safety success and native-exact parity use separate denominators.

Native path-error status/presentation is profile-sensitive: default native file may
print diagnostics on stdout and exit zero. Preserve recorded statuses and diagnostic
meaning; do not require literal errno codes in virtual stderr or downgrade unknown
failures to successful empty files. Native denied-path result depends on actual host
credentials; retained observation is not an invented universal permission oracle.

No memory/RSS benchmark or claim of zero upstream allocation: an oversized supplied
chunk already exists. Bounded prefix tests constrain consumed/retained useful bytes
and further next calls, not opaque provider prefetch. Unknown stat size is modeled
as ENOTSUP, not an invalid FileStat. readFile maxBytes is a whole-file guard, not a
prefix protocol. Cancellation doesn't stop arbitrary uncooperative host promises.
Namespace races do not impose snapshots, transactions, leases or rollback.

Review assertions against the frozen user/contracts before routing failures. A
genuine harness defect requires an additive correction record with original failure,
fixture, oracle and hashes retained; never rewrite the oracle because candidate
fails. Scope unsupported formats/options honestly without claiming they passed.
Only root reveals minimal legitimate reproductions to the author after frozen run.

Before release acceptance, separately audit product runtime dependencies, subprocess
use, implicit host access/libmagic, decompression and public exports/registration.
PREP cannot establish these from zero product runs; the canary covers one path only.
No backend deployment, universal parity, just-bash superiority or task completion
claim follows from this scoped holdout.
